THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

Typefaces. The four faces the page asks for — Zilla Slab, Source Sans 3,
IBM Plex Mono and Courier Prime — are open-licensed (SIL Open Font License)
and are loaded from Google Fonts at runtime. None of them is bundled in this
repository, and deleting the three <link> tags in src/shell.html leaves the
program working on the fallback stacks with no external requests at all.

Final Draft. "Final Draft" is a trademark of Final Draft, Inc. This project is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from Final Draft; it reads and
writes the .fdx file format and refers to the program's keyboard behaviour for
compatibility.

Fountain. The .fountain syntax is a public plain-text screenplay format
(fountain.io), implemented here independently.

The craft material. The guide paraphrases, summarises and occasionally quotes
standard screenwriting references — Syd Field, Blake Snyder, Robert McKee,
Lajos Egri, John Yorke, John Truby, Christopher Riley and others — with each
source named where its idea is used, as a set of working notes does. Those
authors retain all rights in their own work. Redistributing this guide would
put that material in front of people who have not bought those books, which is
a further reason this repository is not open.
